p of the staff, matching Bb4 Eb5 D5 C5 | Bb4 C5 Bb4 C5. Bar 29: a single quarter (Bb4), a quarter rest and a half rest. This is the distinctive bar that anchors the count. Bar 30: two more groups of four eighths, the same figure as bar 28. Then come two bars, each holding two open half notes on the first ledger line above the staff (Bb4), with a tremolo stroke through each stem, then the final barline. By position these are bars 31 and 32. But their notes don't match the edition's text. Bar 31 there is Bb4 then seven F4 eighths. Bar 32 is Eb4 and three Bb4 eighths, then a Bb4 tremolo half. The copy's tremolo Bb4 halves look more like bar 33. They don't match bars 33 and 34 either, because bar 34 is on C5 and all four of these heads sit on the same ledger line. So this copy probably has a different reading of bars 31–32, which I can't confirm from the image. The bar sequence 26, 27, 28, 29, 30, then two bars fits only if the line ends at bar 32.","right":true,"insights":"The start was easy to place: the natural on the A/F chords, the quarter plus rest of bar 26, the whole-bar rest and the lone quarter of bar 29 fix it. The end is uncertain. The last two bars hold tremolo Bb4 halves that differ from the edition's bars 31–32, and only counting bars supports bar 32. A look at the start of the next line, or a sharper view of the ledger-line heads (Bb4 or C5), would settle it."},"ttft_ms":35843,"type":"result","duration_ms":43405,"uuid":"88bb275d-c829-4e52-8d82-ad36d397d692","ttft_stream_ms":1921,"time_to_request_ms":517,"first_content_frame_ms":1921,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":3831,"cacheReadInputTokens":523,"cacheCreationInputTokens":5395,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.11989259999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3037,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":5395,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","p